.TH TENSOR-GPU-QUEUE 1 "November 2026" "Tensor GPU Queue Stage 1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensor-gpu-queue \- simulate persistent GPU job admission without executing inference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ~/ops/shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-queue.py
.RI [ --db " FILE" ] " COMMAND " [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stage 1 of the Tensor GPU inference lifecycle. Maintains a private, SQLite-backed
queue for synthetic fixture jobs. Does not execute arbitrary commands, GPUs,
Hermes, MinerU, Ollama, Qdrant, systemd, or Wallpaper Engine operations.
All job activity checks are SIMULATED and manually supplied by the operator.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show paused state and aggregate job counts.
.TP
.B list [--limit N]
List job IDs and state, without printing sources or private errors.
.TP
.B submit --source FIXTURE [--priority N] [--max-attempts N]
Create/reuse one synthetic job. Same source is deduplicated, including after completion.
.TP
.B submit-batch [--prefix FIXTURE] [--count N]
Atomically submit 1 to 1000 synthetic jobs; default is 30.
.TP
.B run-synthetic [--activity idle|active|unknown] [--limit N]
Run only synthetic jobs, never real GPU work. Default activity is unknown,
which refuses admission. Active and paused also refuse admission.
.TP
.B recover
Recover expired worker leases; uncertain prior attempts are retried or marked failed,
never silently acknowledged as completed.
.TP
.B pause | resume
Persistently stop or permit new claims; existing running work is not killed.
.TP
.B cancel JOB_ID | retry JOB_ID
Cancel pending/retry/failed jobs or manually retry failed jobs. Running jobs are protected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/tensor-gpu-queue/queue.sqlite3
Private durable queue database; directory requires mode 0700, database mode 0600.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/tensor-gpu-queue/worker.lock
Advisory one-worker lock.
.SH SAFETY
No inference adapters or automatic idle triggers are installed in Stage 1.
File paths, logs, and database content must not be committed to public Git.
A lease does not prove exactly-once external effects after process failure;
future real workload adapters must enforce idempotent output and checkpoint recovery.
.SH SEE ALSO
~/ops/docs/plans/tensor-gpu-inference-lifecycle.md
